Persist fake-IP mappings and allocation state in one synchronous transaction.
Downstream change based on upstream mihomo:
https://github.com/MetaCubeX/mihomo/blob/Alpha/component/fakeip/pool.go
https://github.com/MetaCubeX/mihomo/blob/Alpha/component/profile/cachefile/fakeip.go

Allocate from the committed database cursor, replace both mapping directions,
remove the previous address owner and save the offset/wrap marker in one Update.
This avoids the default Batch delay while retaining synchronous persistence.

Read both state fields from one snapshot. Preserve caches without a shutdown
checkpoint and skip their occupied addresses on the first new allocation.
Shutdown no longer writes a stale local cursor over another resolver's progress.
The bucket names, mapping layout and state keys remain compatible with old cores.

Tests cover rollback, atomic reader snapshots, IPv4/IPv6, legacy checkpoints,
reload with overlapping resolvers, and restart after killing a child process.
Includes standalone before/after benchmarks using synthetic temporary databases.
Includes a 500-record correctness test and 500-record benchmark fixtures.
Performance and restart audit: benchmarks/fakeip-atomic-write.md.
500-record follow-up: benchmarks/fakeip-500.md.

